 F.1,"Sections, torsors, and local conditions — Let $k$ be a number field, $X/k$ a smooth geometrically connected curve, and $b$ a rational point or rational tangential point. For a characteristic quotient $U$ of the geometric fundamental group, the section at $b$ identifies the corresponding arithmetic extension with $U\rtimes G_k$. Continuous splittings modulo conjugation by $U$ are the pointed set $H^1_{\rm cts}(G_k,U)$. For a unipotent $\Q_p$-group $U$, a Selmer scheme is a specified subset of this pointed set, cut out by ramification and local conditions. It is not the unrestricted set of splittings.",Proved,"sections/F.tex, F.1",,Section 51; folio 734;736; scan 173;178 (cote 140-4),No,"Full claim, assumptions and proof or recorded residual attack are in the indicated source."
 F.2,"All standard tripod dimensions through class eight — Put $X=\mathbb P^1_\Q\setminus\{0,1,\infty\}$ and use the unit tangent at $0$. Let $S$ be a finite set of rational primes, $s=|S|$, and choose $p\ge5$ outside $S$. For $U_n=\pi_1^{\rm un}(X_{\overline\Q},b)/\gamma_{n+1}$ over $\Q_p$, impose unramifiedness outside $S\cup\{p\}$ and crystallinity at $p$. Write $\operatorname{Sel}_{S,n}$ for this standard Selmer scheme, without additional refined conditions at $S$. Then \[ \begin{split} \dim\operatorname{Sel}_{S,n} &=2s+\sum_{\substack{3\le j\le n\\j\ {\rm odd}}}\ell_j(2),\\ \dim H_f^1(\Q_p,U_n)&=\sum_{j=1}^n\ell_j(2),\\ \ell_j(2)&=\frac1j\sum_{d\mid j}\mu(d)2^{j/d}. \end{split} \] The first formula includes $n=1$. In particular:",Proved,"sections/F.tex, F.2",B.12,"Section 51, equations (371)-(373); folios 734 and 736; scans 173 and 178; explicit Selmer tasks in prompt Part F",No,"Full claim, assumptions and proof or recorded residual attack are in the indicated source."
 F.3,"The first dimension drops and integral finiteness — For each of $U_n$ and $M_n$, the first strict inequality \[ \dim\operatorname{Sel}_{S,n}<\dim H_f^1(\Q_p,U_n) \] (with $M_n$ substituted in its case) occurs at class $1,2,4$ for $s=0,1,2$, respectively. Each inequality implies that $X(\Z[1/S])$ is finite. It does not identify that set with the corresponding Selmer locus.",Known,"sections/F.tex, F.3",F.2,"Section 51, equations (371)-(373); folios 734 and 736; scans 173 and 178; explicit Selmer tasks in prompt Part F",No,"Full claim, assumptions and proof or recorded residual attack are in the indicated source."
 F.4,"Abelian approximations do not separate every cusp — For the tripod the unrestricted abelian section sets are \[ H^1(G_\Q,\widehat\Z(1)^2) =\left(\varprojlim_m\Q^\times/(\Q^\times)^m\right)^2, \qquad H^1(G_\Q,\Q_p(1)^2) =\left(\widehat{\Q^\times}^{\,p}\otimes_{\Z_p}\Q_p\right)^2. \] They are infinite. The two tangential sections at $0$ and $1$, using respectively parameters $z$ and $1-z$ with unit tangent, have the same class in both sets. Thus the assertion that distinct cusps remain nonconjugate in every abelian approximation is false. This counterexample concerns an approximation, and does not identify the full profinite cuspidal sections.",Refuted,"sections/F.tex, F.4",F.2,"Section 51, equations (371)-(373); folios 734 and 736; scans 173 and 178; explicit Selmer tasks in prompt Part F",No,"Full claim, assumptions and proof or recorded residual attack are in the indicated source."
-F.5,"The effect of the degree-seven nonpentagonal element — Let $\ell\ge5$ and let $\beta$ be the pro-$\ell$ element of B.12 with normalized conjugator $f$ having leading Lie term $q_7$. On $U_n$ it is the identity for $n\le7$. In class eight, with the normalization $\beta(x)=x,\ \beta(y)=f^{-1}yf$, its first change is \[ \beta(\log x)=\log x,\qquad \beta(\log y)=\log y+[\log y,q_7]\pmod{\text{degree}>8}. \] It transports cocycles for $\rho$ bijectively to cocycles for $\rho^\beta=\beta\rho\beta^{-1}$. It need not act on the section set for the \emph{fixed} action $\rho$. All tripod finiteness thresholds in F.3 occur before this change can be detected.",Proved,"sections/F.tex, F.5",,"Section 51, equations (371)-(373); folios 734 and 736; scans 173 and 178; explicit Selmer tasks in prompt Part F",No,"Full claim, assumptions and proof or recorded residual attack are in the indicated source."
